There is an explicitly specified entangled density operator $\rho$ on $\mathbb C^{10}\otimes\mathbb C^{10}$ whose range contains no nonzero product vector and for which $K_D(\rho)=0$. More precisely, let $n\geq1$ and let $\tau_{K_AK_BE'}$ be the normalized output of any admitted completed bit-output protocol of Definition <a href="#def:protocol" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="def:protocol">[def:protocol]</a> on $\rho^{\otimes n}$, where $E'$ retains an initial purification and the complete public transcript. For every state $\sigma_{E'}$, $$\label{eq:main-gap}
 \left\lVert \tau_{K_AK_BE'}-
 \frac12\sum_{i=0}^1|i,i\rangle\langle i,i|\otimes\sigma_{E'}
 \right\rVert_1\geq\frac15.$$ Thus the corresponding trace distance, with its conventional factor $1/2$, is at least $1/10$.

Let $F:M_{a}(\mathbb C)\to M_{b}(\mathbb C)$ and $G:M_{b}(\mathbb C)\to M_{c}(\mathbb C)$ be CP maps, and set $F^\sharp=T_a\circ F^\dagger\circ T_b$. Then $$\label{eq:choi-transfer}
 J(G\circ F)=(F^\sharp\otimes G)(\Omega_b\Omega_b^*).$$ If $F$ and $G$ are PPT and $Z=J(G\circ F)\ne0$, then $\lambda:=\operatorname{tr}Z>0$ and $$\label{eq:choi-transfer-normalized}
 \frac{Z}{\lambda}
 =(F^\sharp\otimes G)
 \left(\frac{\Omega_b\Omega_b^*}{\lambda}\right)\in\mathscr C
 \quad\text{on }\mathbb C^a\otimes\mathbb C^c.$$

Let $\omega\in\mathscr C$ act on $\mathbb C^p\otimes\mathbb C^q$. For arbitrary $X_0,X_1\succeq0$ in $M_{p}(\mathbb C)$ and $Y_0,Y_1\succeq0$ in $M_{q}(\mathbb C)$, put $$D_{ij}=X_i\otimes Y_j,
 \qquad p_{ij}=\operatorname{tr}(D_{ij}\omega),
 \qquad i,j\in\{0,1\}.$$ Then $$\label{eq:coherence}
 \left\lVert\sqrt{D_{00}}\,\omega\sqrt{D_{11}}\right\rVert_1
 \le \sqrt{p_{00}p_{01}}+\sqrt{p_{10}p_{11}}
       +2\sqrt{p_{01}p_{10}}.$$ There is no normalization assumption on $X_0,X_1,Y_0,Y_1$.

For arbitrary square complex matrices $A,B$ of the same size, $$\label{eq:polar-fidelity}
 f(A^*A,B^*B)=\left\lVert AB^*\right\rVert_1.$$ For positive matrices $H,J$ of the same size, $$\label{eq:fidelity-lower}
 f(H,J)\ge
 \frac{\operatorname{tr}H+\operatorname{tr}J-\left\lVert H-J\right\rVert_1}{2}.$$ Also $f(H^\mathsf T,J^\mathsf T)=f(H,J)$.

Let $\omega\in\mathscr C$. For every integer $n\ge1$, let an admitted completed protocol on $\omega^{\otimes n}$ produce normalized bit registers $K_A,K_B$, and let its output $\tau_{K_AK_BE'}$ retain in $E'$ an initial purification held by Eve and the complete public transcript. The purification may be arbitrary. For every normalized state or classical-quantum law $\sigma_{E'}$, $$\label{eq:uniform-secret-bit-gap}
 \left\lVert\tau_{K_AK_BE'}-
  \frac12\sum_{i=0}^1|i,i\rangle\langle i,i|\otimes\sigma_{E'}
 \right\rVert_1\ge\frac15.$$ Thus the conventional trace distance is at least $1/10$, and $K_D(\omega)=0$ in Definition <a href="#def:distillable-key" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="def:distillable-key">15</a>.

Let $\Psi_1,\Psi_2:M_{m}(\mathbb C)\to M_{m}(\mathbb C)$ be PPT maps. There are explicitly defined constants $c_1,c_2>0$, a trace-preserving PPT channel $\Theta:M_{2m+1}(\mathbb C)\to M_{2m+1}(\mathbb C)$, and a real coordinate isometry $W_0:\mathbb C^m\to\mathbb C^{2m+1}$ such that $$\label{eq:choi-corner}
 (W_0^*\otimes W_0^*)J(\Theta\circ\Theta)(W_0\otimes W_0)
       =c_1c_2J(\Psi_2\circ\Psi_1).$$ If $J(\Psi_2\circ\Psi_1)$ is nonseparable, then $\Theta\circ\Theta$ is not entanglement breaking.

Let $Q,K,D$ be positive integers, let $\mathcal Q$ be a set of $Q$ elements, and let $u_q\in\mathbb R^K$, $q\in\mathcal Q$, be unit vectors. Put $c_{qr}=u_q^{\mathsf T}u_r$. For each $q$, let $\{P_i:i\in\mathcal I_q\}$ be a finite projective measurement on $\mathbb C^D$: its members are self-adjoint projections, they are mutually orthogonal, and their sum is $I_D$. Zero projections are allowed. Take the label sets $\mathcal I_q$ disjoint, put $\mathcal I=\bigsqcup_{q\in\mathcal Q}\mathcal I_q$, and set $n=|\mathcal I|$. Suppose that*

1.  *$P_iP_j=P_jP_i$ whenever $i\in\mathcal I_q$, $j\in\mathcal I_r$, and $c_{qr}\ne0$;*

2.  *there is a real number $\kappa<Q/K$ such that every $J\subseteq\mathcal I$ satisfying $\operatorname{tr}(P_iP_j)>0$ for all distinct $i,j\in J$ has $|J|\leq\kappa$.*


*After ordering $\mathcal I$, define the complex-linear map $\Psi:M_{n}(\mathbb C)\to M_{D}(\mathbb C)$ on matrix units by $$\label{eq:projection-map}
 H_{ij}=c_{qr}P_iP_j,\qquad
 \Psi(E_{ij})=H_{ij}
 \quad(i\in\mathcal I_q,\ j\in\mathcal I_r).$$ Then $\Psi$ and its Hilbert–Schmidt adjoint $\Psi^\dagger:M_{D}(\mathbb C)\to M_{n}(\mathbb C)$ are PPT. Moreover, $$\label{eq:projection-composite}
 C:=J(\Psi^\dagger\circ\Psi)
 \quad\text{is nonseparable over }\mathbb C^n\otimes\mathbb C^n,
 \qquad \operatorname{tr}C=Q^2D.$$

Under the hypotheses of Proposition <a href="#prop:projection-criterion" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:projection-criterion">26</a>, suppose that every $P_i$ is real symmetric in the fixed basis of $\mathbb C^D$, and put $\Lambda=\Psi^\dagger:M_{D}(\mathbb C)\to M_{n}(\mathbb C)$. Then, on all complex inputs, $$\label{eq:projection-real-invariances}
 \Lambda\circ T_D=\Lambda=T_n\circ\Lambda,
 \qquad \operatorname{tr}\Lambda(A)=Q\,\operatorname{tr}A.$$ In particular, $\Lambda/Q$ is a trace-preserving PPT channel. For $\Phi_D=\Omega_D/\sqrt D$, the normalized maximally entangled vector on $\mathbb C^D\otimes\mathbb C^D$, one has $$\label{eq:projection-real-state}
 \frac{C}{Q^2D}
 =
 \left(\frac{\Lambda}{Q}\otimes\frac{\Lambda}{Q}\right)
       (\Phi_D\Phi_D^*).$$ This is an entangled density operator on $\mathbb C^n\otimes\mathbb C^n$ in $\mathscr C$.

Under the hypotheses of Proposition <a href="#prop:projection-criterion" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:projection-criterion">26</a>, suppose in addition that $n\geq D$, and let $U:\mathbb C^D\to\mathbb C^n$ be the real coordinate isometry onto the first $D$ coordinates. Define $$\label{eq:projection-square-pair}
 \Xi_1=\operatorname{Ad}_U\circ\Psi,\qquad
 \Xi_2=\Psi^\dagger\circ\operatorname{Ad}_{U^*}
       =\Xi_1^\dagger .$$ Then $\Xi_1,\Xi_2:M_{n}(\mathbb C)\to M_{n}(\mathbb C)$ are PPT and $$\Xi_2\circ\Xi_1=\Psi^\dagger\circ\Psi.$$ Their composition is not entanglement breaking.
